how do you speak truth to power when you  work in an environment where speaking  truth to power can get you fired or  could get you in trouble one of the  reasons that happens is not because  we're necessarily speaking truth to  power it's the manner in which we do it  we usually do it as a complaint or we do  it as an aggressive question and we also  do without empathy one of the most  important things to do is have empathy  for the people who we work for we don't  know what their story is we don't know  what kind of pressure they're under we  don't know if they're operating from a  point of fear and so when we come in  guns a-blazing their walls are gonna go  up because we're aggressive or we're  perceived as aggressive so if you can  maintain empathy and some curiosity and  work hard to spend the time to build a  relationship with with that person in  that authority position so they  understand that we want to see them  succeed and I want to ask you some  questions because if you can ask these  questions hi I can be more successful  which is gonna help you be more  successful or to say things like are you  okay or to say things like hey you would  really harsh to us on the meeting today  I just want to check in with you is  everything okay these are little things  we can do to think about them as human  beings rather than oppressors and to  operate with as much empathy and  curiosity as possible and hopefully  build that relationship so they see us  as trust and trusting and amazingly  they'll probably open up and you'll  learn a lot more so that that works  [Music]
 

